  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "FISHER computes 0.5 * LN((1+x)/(1-x)) with stored 1+x and 1-x, collapsing tiny |x| < 2^-53 to 0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20430, FISHER(x) rejects |x| >= 1 with #NUM! and evaluates 0.5 * LN(RN53(RN64(1 + x)) / RN53(RN64(1 - x))) using stored binary64 values for 1 + x and 1 - x rather than ATANH(x)'s small-x cubic series or 0.5 * (LN(1 + x) - LN(1 - x)). Consequently, for any |x| < 2^-53 (such as 1e-16 or 1e-300), both 1 + x and 1 - x round to 1 and FISHER(x) returns 0 instead of atanh(x) ~= x. All 5,697 full-bank FISHER rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-extended-numeric-20260929/answers/answers-fisher.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and matched on 5,697/5,697 full-bank rows (33/33 signed small-input discriminators vs 21/33 for ATANH and 10/33 for split LN).",
